# DocuMate settings.
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values. .env is gitignored;
# this template is not, so never put the real password in here.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Read automatically when python-dotenv is installed. Without it this file
# is ignored and the values fall back to real environment variables, so
# setting them in your shell works too:
#
#     setx DOCUMATE_DB_PASSWORD "your-password"      (Windows, new shells)
#     export DOCUMATE_DB_PASSWORD="your-password"    (bash)


# --- Database, for versions Z and O ----------------------------------------
# All four are required. If one is missing DocuMate stops straight away and
# tells you which, instead of failing later with a confusing error.
#
# These used to be written into src/DocuMateZ.py and src/DocuMateO.py. Those
# files were tracked by git, so the connection details went to GitHub with
# every push. They live here now.

DOCUMATE_DB_HOST=
DOCUMATE_DB_NAME=postgres
DOCUMATE_DB_USER=
DOCUMATE_DB_PASSWORD=
DOCUMATE_DB_PORT=5432
DOCUMATE_DB_SSLMODE=require

# Supabase note: the direct db.<project-ref>.supabase.co host needs IPv6, or
# the paid IPv4 add-on. On an IPv4-only network use the Session pooler host
# from Project Settings -> Database -> Connection string instead. The pooler
# also changes the user to postgres.<project-ref>.


# --- Excel, for versions v3, X and Y ---------------------------------------
# Both optional. Defaults are data/DocuMate_DataFrame.xlsx and DocuMateSRC.

# DOCUMATE_EXCEL_PATH=
# DOCUMATE_SHEET_NAME=DocuMateSRC


# --- Other -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Project folder override. Normally leave this alone - DocuMate works it out
# from where it is running. Useful for testing.

# DOCUMATE_ROOT=

# Set to 0 to print messages to the console instead of showing Windows
# popups. Happens automatically when not on Windows.

# DOCUMATE_POPUPS=1
